# E429 draft — OHAudio selects the actual callback frame quantum
id:                     E429-draft-A6F1
trigger_tool:           OHAudio|HarmonyOS NDK|Conan|runtime
phase:                  stream-creation|audio-callback|target-validation
error_signature:        callback frame count mismatch|requested frame count differs from OHAudio callback size|OH_AudioRenderer_GetFrameSizeInCallback|OH_AudioCapturer_GetFrameSizeInCallback

severity:               2
category:               ohos, runtime, testing, audio
match_keywords:         OHAudio, OH_AudioRenderer_GetFrameSizeInCallback, OH_AudioCapturer_GetFrameSizeInCallback, callback frame size, bufferFrames, requested frames, RtAudio
title:                  Query the device-selected OHAudio callback frame size after stream creation

root_cause:             The frame count requested while building an OHAudio stream is not necessarily the frame quantum selected by the device. On the tested HarmonyOS PC, the request was 480 frames and OHAudio selected 960 frames. A backend that keeps sizing buffers or reporting RtAudio bufferFrames from the request can process the wrong number of samples per callback, misreport delivered frames, or access beyond the allocated device buffer.
affected_scope:         HarmonyOS/OHOS applications and audio backends using OHAudio renderer or capturer callbacks, especially adapters that expose a requested bufferFrames value to a cross-platform audio API.
verification_cmd:       On an AArch64 HarmonyOS device, create renderer and capturer streams with a 480-frame request, query each created stream with its GetFrameSizeInCallback API, allocate and process using the returned frame count, and verify callback frame totals and buffer byte sizes against that value.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           query-device-selected-ohaudio-callback-quantum
rec_description:        After creating each renderer or capturer, query its actual callback frame size, reject query errors or zero, publish that value as the stream bufferFrames, and size callback buffers from actual frames times channels and sample width with overflow checks.
rec_command:            Create OHAudio stream -> GetFrameSizeInCallback -> allocate and report using the returned frame count
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               OHOS OHAudio backend

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      reject-stream-without-valid-callback-size
fallback_description:   If the platform cannot provide a valid callback frame size, fail stream creation with a diagnostic; do not assume the requested frame count is the delivered callback quantum.
fallback_command:       Check the GetFrameSizeInCallback result before allocating or starting the stream.
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          OHAudio stream validation

forbid_1_pattern:       bufferFrames[[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*requestedFrames
forbid_1_reason:        OHAudio can select a callback quantum different from the requested size.
forbid_1_consequence:   Callback buffers can be undersized and reported frame counts can disagree with the frames delivered by the device.
forbid_2_pattern:       allocate.*requestedFrames
forbid_2_reason:        Device callback storage must follow the created stream's actual frame quantum.
forbid_2_consequence:   The callback can read or write outside a buffer sized only from the request.

